        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: பொருளாதாரம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பொருளாதாரம் — poruḷātāram — \"the economy\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "மழை பெய்யாவிட்டால் நாட்டின் பொருளாதாரம் பாதிக்கப்படும். maḻai peyyāviṭṭāl nāṭṭiṉ poruḷātāram pātikkappaṭum. If it does not rain, the country's economy will suffer."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பொருளாதார, economic, before a noun: பொருளாதார வளர்ச்சி, economic growth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "பொருளாதாரம் (poruḷātāram) is built from native poruḷ, \"thing, wealth\" (DEDR 4544), and ātāram, \"support, basis\", borrowed from Sanskrit ādhāra (CDIAL 1165): what wealth rests on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
